jobs.description:
For our client in the DIKSMUIDE area, we are looking for a SHEET METAL WORKER.

Our client is a company where employees are at the heart of the business and where everyone is given the opportunity to develop their skills and receive further training. 

Since 1957, the company has been a leading metalworking company serving Belgium, the Netherlands, Luxembourg and Northern France.

As a PLATE WORKER in the DIKSMUIDE area, your responsibilities will include:

• You will be flexibly deployed within the sheet metal department according to the needs of the planning;
• You operate and set up machines for laser cutting, bending and rolling sheet metal;
• You prepare the necessary programs and machine settings and check that the machines are functioning correctly;
• You perform some basic administrative tasks, such as receiving incoming sheets, checking stock and entering the information into the system;
• You ensure the proper finishing of the parts, including deburring and quality control;
• You independently move sheets and finished parts using a forklift.
What does our client in the DIKSMUIDE area expect from a new SHEET METAL WORKER colleague?

• You have experience in sheet metal processing and preferably have experience with several of the following techniques: laser cutting, bending, nesting and rolling;
• You have a valid forklift certificate;
• You can read technical drawings and work accurately;
• You speak Dutch or English;
• You have completed a technical education (A2 level), for example in mechanics or metalworking, or have equivalent experience.

Do you have a passion for cars and take pride in restoring vehicle bodywork to perfection? Do you enjoy working accurately and have a keen eye for detail?

For a modern, well-equipped garage in Jabbeke, we are looking for an experienced Vehicle Body Repair to strengthen the team.

As a VEHICLE BODY REPAIRER in JABBEKE, your responsibilities will include:

• Repairing damaged vehicles;
• Assembling and disassembling bodywork parts, interior components and mechanical parts;
• Repairing body panels through dent removal, shrinking and stretching techniques;
• Carrying out straightening and pulling work to repair more complex bodywork damage;
• Preparing vehicles to ensure a smooth finish, ready for painting;
• Checking the quality of your own work and maintaining a clean and safe working environment.
As a BODYWORKER in the JABBEKE region, you meet the following requirements:

• You have at least 5 years of experience in the automotive sector as a panel beater or vehicle body repair technician;
• You speak Dutch OR English;
• You have a Category B driving licence.

Our client is a leading international trading and supply chain organization with a long-established presence across Europe and a strong global footprint. Active in the distribution and trading of industrial and chemical products, the company combines commercial expertise, logistics capabilities, and financial strength to support international business operations.

Jobomschrijving

As Senior Accountant, you will play a key role in ensuring the accuracy of accounting operations, compliance, and financial reporting within an international business environment. Working closely with a Shared Service Center and stakeholders across Europe, your responsibilities will include:

• Managing monthly, quarterly, and annual closing activities, including accruals, reconciliations, and balance sheet reviews;
• Acting as the accounting reference point for the Belgian entity and overseeing the quality of accounting transactions processed by the Shared Service Center;
• Taking ownership of VAT compliance, tax-related reporting, and statutory obligations across multiple European jurisdictions;
• Coordinating annual audits and supporting the preparation of statutory financial statements;
• Partnering with business teams to provide accounting and tax guidance on commercial and operational activities;
• Ensuring compliance with local regulations, internal controls, and group accounting policies;
• Identifying opportunities to streamline processes, strengthen controls, and drive continuous improvement initiatives;
• Contributing to digitization and automation projects, including the adoption of innovative technologies and AI-driven solutions;

We are looking for a collaborative and flexible professional who enjoys taking ownership and working in a team-oriented environment. The ideal candidate combines technical accounting expertise with a strong process improvement mindset and has an interest in digital transformation and emerging technologies such as AI.

• Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field;
• Minimum 4 years of accounting experience within an international or B2B environment;
• Strong understanding of Belgian GAAP and VAT regulations;
• Experience with statutory accounting and external audits;
• Knowledge of SAP S/4HANA or SAP Hana is considered a strong asset;
• Fluent in English and French; Dutch is a plus;
• Analytical, detail-oriented, and process-minded;
• Comfortable working with multiple stakeholders in an international environment;
• Proactive, hands-on, and eager to contribute to continuous improvement initiatives;
